        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: परिवारः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "परिवारः — parivāraḥ — \"a household, a family\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "parivāra is built on pari, \"around\", and the root √vṛ, \"to cover, surround\" (MW). It first meant \"cover, surroundings\", then \"followers\" (CDIAL 7876), and Hindi took it as parivār, \"family\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
